    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.bufremove\n\n### Description\n\nI often face a situation where `MiniBufremove.wipeout()` is followed by `:tabclose` or `<C-w>c`.\n\nWouldn't it be great to combine both in the single action? For example, if user has:\n```lua\nMiniBufremove.config = {\n      close_tab = true,\n      close_split = true\n  }\n```\n\nThen `wipeout()` would _also_ close the active tab and split. Alternatively, these can be made function arguments.\n\nThoughts? ",
